}],"config":{"leagueName":"Harbor City","currentSeason":2026,"formatValue":"12-team","formatNote":"Auction keeper league","eras":[{"years":"2011\u20132021","text":"THE CONSOLATION BRACKET ERA"},{"years":"2022\u2013Present","text":"THE TOILET BOWL ERA"}],"coverageNote":"Final standings go back to 2011. Detailed matchup records begin with the 2022 Sleeper season.","annals":{"eyebrow":"The League Annals","title":"Our Story: Harbor City","paragraphs":["**Harbor City FFL** was born in 2011 at a dockside bar, when ten friends decided an auction draft was the only fair way to settle who knew football best.","Twelve teams have played every season since 2012. Each team gets a $200 budget, keeps up to two players at last year's price plus $10, and plays in one of three divisions.","Final standings go all the way back to 2011. Game-by-game records begin when the league moved to Sleeper in 2022."],"callout":null,"memoriam":null},"lore":{"intro":"The stories, rulings and legends behind the league.","entries":[{"year":"2012","title":"The $1 Kicker","text":"A sleepy owner bid $1 on a kicker at 2 a.m. He won the auction, the kicker, and the title.","note":null},{"year":"League curse","title":"The #2 Seed Curse","text":"Earn the No. 2 seed, enjoy the bye, and lose in the semifinals. It has happened more often than anyone can explain.","note":null},{"year":"2022","title":"Birth of the Toilet Bowl","text":"The league voted in a last-place bracket in 2022. The loser runs the next auction in a sailor hat.","note":null},{"year":"2025","title":"Points-For Seeds","text":"The owners voted to give the last two playoff spots to the top points-for teams. The vote passed 9\u20133.","note":null}]},"exploreLinks":[{"label":"Weekly recaps","href":"/recaps"},{"label":"Rivalries","href":"/league-info/rivalries"},{"label":"Records","href":"/league-info/records"},{"label":"Managers","href":"/managers"},{"label":"Draft history","href":"/league-info/drafts"}],"activeFranchises":[{"franchiseId":"tidewate